#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:311
msgid "Common Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:313
msgid ""
"**Don't use `informed` as default** — it's experimental and slower. Use "
"`advanced` for reliable results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:314
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Models under ~1B respond poorly to abliteration** — their refusal "
"behaviors are shallow and fragmented, making clean direction extraction "
"difficult. Expect partial results (20-40% remaining refusal). Models 3B+ "
"have cleaner refusal directions and respond much better (often 0% refusal"
" with `advanced`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:315
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**`aggressive` can make things worse** — on small models it can damage "
"coherence and actually increase refusal rate. Only use it if `advanced` "
"leaves > 10% refusals on a 3B+ model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:316
msgid ""
"**Always check perplexity** — if it spikes > 15%, the model is damaged. "
"Reduce aggressiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:317
msgid ""
"**MoE models need special handling** — use `nuclear` method for Mixtral, "
"DeepSeek-MoE, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:318
msgid ""
"**Quantized models can't be re-quantized** — abliterate the full-"
"precision model, then quantize the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:319
msgid ""
"**VRAM estimation is approximate** — 4-bit quant helps but peak usage can"
" spike during extraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:320
msgid ""
"**Reasoning models are sensitive** — use `surgical` for R1 distills to "
"preserve chain-of-thought."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:321
msgid ""
"**Check `obliteratus recommend`** — telemetry data may have better "
"parameters than defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:322
msgid ""
"**AGPL license** — never `import obliteratus` in MIT/Apache projects. CLI"
" invocation only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:323
msgid ""
"**Large models (70B+)** — always use `--large-model` flag for "
"conservative defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/obliteratus_SKILL.md:324
msgid ""
"**Spectral certification RED is common** — the spectral check often flags"
